 $\\$7.50\\,.$\n\n- Bag $B$ weighs $2$ kilograms, and costs $\\$3.20\\,.$\n\n- Bag $C$ weighs $1$ kilogram, and costs $\\$1.70\\,.$\n\nWhich bag of flour is the best deal?" 13194139539468 17592186576411 true] [17592186495092 1074 "The best deal is the one with the lowest unit price. So, we need to compute the unit prices for all three bags. To compute the unit price, we divide the cost by the total number of kilograms.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of kilograms in bag $A$, we get\n\n$$\n7.50÷5=1.50\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $A$ is $$1.50$ per kilogram.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of kilograms in bag $B$, we get\n\n$$\n3.20÷2=1.60\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $B$ is $$1.60$ per kilogram.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of kilograms in bag $C$, we get\n\n$$\n1.70÷1=1.70\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $C$ is $$1.70$ per kilogram.\n\nFrom the above, we see that bag $A$ has the lowest unit price. Therefore, bag $A$ is the best deal." 13194139539468 17592186576411 false] [17592186495092 1074 "The best deal is the one with the lowest unit price. So, we need to compute the unit prices for all three bags. To compute the unit price, we divide the cost by the total number of kilograms.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of kilograms in bag $A$, we get\n\n$$\n7.50÷5=1.50\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $A$ is $\\$1.50$ per kilogram.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of kilograms in bag $B$, we get\n\n$$\n3.20÷2=1.60\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $B$ is $\\$1.60$ per kilogram.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of kilograms in bag $C$, we get\n\n$$\n1.70÷1=1.70\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $C$ is $\\$1.70$ per kilogram.\n\nFrom the above, we see that bag $A$ has the lowest unit price. Therefore, bag $A$ is the best deal." 13194139539468 17592186576411 true] [17592186495093 1071 "Lucy wants to make a cake and is going to buy some fruit to decorate. How much would it cost h